  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a long press on an image link in a message to offer \"Ouvrir l'image\" (in the app's image viewer) and \"Enregistrer dans Photos\", as the legacy app did, so that the link menu of #596 does not lose them.\n\n### Scope\n- Legacy: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:1241-1249` @ 2440d79 (context menu on image links: open in the viewer, save to Photos).\n- PR #607 (#596) adds the long-press menu for links (Ouvrir, Copier, Safari, app) and drops the image-link entries; its GAP row records them as deferred to this issue.\n- Add the two entries when the long-pressed element is an image link (or image), reusing the reader's image viewer and the cookie-less image client (policy C). Saving needs the add-only Photos permission (`NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription`): check what the app target already declares.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Long press on an image link shows the #596 entries plus \"Ouvrir l'image\" and \"Enregistrer dans Photos\".\n- The image is fetched through the existing image path (no session cookies sent to third-party hosts).\n- Swift Testing tests for the menu composition; Mac check on device for the save.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator: nothing from the device feedback goes to M5). Found by device testing (#596).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
